From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Erich Seifert <dev@erichseifert.de>
Date: Sun, 27 Sep 2026 14:34:33 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 2/9] Record bin clips in a PostProject sidecar on save

Saving film.kdenlive records each file-backed bin clip in film.pproj:
an imported asset with PostProject's content fingerprint, keyed by
kdenlive:control_uuid, with Kdenlive's own clip hash kept as a host
fingerprint and recorded together with an observation of the clip's
content. A clip Kdenlive relinked gets its new location confirmed, and
former locations whose files are gone are retired. The project file is
not changed, and failures are only logged.

The PostProject C++ wrapper returns results instead of throwing, so the
adapter builds with Kdenlive's default -fno-exceptions.

